  "text_input": "Patient presented with a 3-day history of fever with chills, followed by acute onset of loose stools (8 episodes/day, watery, non-bloody) and vomiting (8 episodes/day). On admission, the patient was hypotensive (BP 80/30 mmHg) and tachycardic (Pulse 102/min), requiring CCU admission. Investigations revealed dimorphic anemia with thrombocytopenia and mild hyperbilirubinemia (Total Bilirubin 1.6 mg/dL). 2D Echo showed normal cardiac function (EF 58%). The patient was diagnosed with acute gastroenteritis and folic acid deficiency anemia. Treatment included IV antibiotics (Ciplox, Metrogyl), IV fluids, and a PRBC transfusion. The patient improved symptomatically and was discharged on oral medications.",
